Start
/ snapshot: every item serializes itself through its own wire; a resume snapshot and an app snapshot. Each stage
/ is a goal; each behaviour a comment with the test that proves it. The coder rewrites each test in plang that compiles.
- call goal Stage1
- call goal Stage2
- call goal Stage3
- call goal Stage4

Stage1
/ One door.
/ A snapshot holds a section for each item that marks members for it, under the item's own path, and none for an item that marks none
- call goal /snapshot/SectionsAreTheItemsOwn
/ A snapshot written to text and read back holds the same entries (its own wire, no other serializer)
- call goal /snapshot/WriteReadRoundTrip
/ An always-fresh value (Now) and a ! name are not captured
- call goal /snapshot/AlwaysFreshNotCaptured

Stage2
/ The resume snapshot.
/ A run that fails at step 3 is saved, written to disk, read back in a fresh app and resumed: it re-enters step 3 with the variables it had
- call goal /snapshot/resume/ResumeAtFailedStep
/ A resume whose goal was rebuilt since (another hash) fails as CallbackGoalHashMismatch
- call goal /snapshot/resume/RebuiltGoalRefuses
/ The variables restored are the ones at the throw, not ones written by the error handler after it
- call goal /snapshot/resume/VariablesAtTheThrow
/ A nested call chain resumes inside the sub-goal, then continues after the call in the parent
- call goal /snapshot/resume/NestedChainResumes

Stage3
/ The app snapshot and children.
/ A child app sees the parent's goals and types without loading them again
- call goal /snapshot/app/ChildSharesParent
/ A module added in a child is not in the parent or a sibling
- call goal /snapshot/app/ChildChangeStaysInChild
/ A dirty child reset matches the parent again
- call goal /snapshot/app/ResetDropsChildChanges

Stage4
/ The callback.
/ A stateless ask's callback carries only the variables the ask gave and its signed position; resumed, the goal continues after the ask
- call goal /snapshot/callback/StatelessAskResumes
/ A stateless callback with its position changed, or past its expiry, is refused
- call goal /snapshot/callback/TamperedOrExpiredRefused
/ A durable resume after an error carries every user variable
- call goal /snapshot/callback/DurableCarriesAll
